      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>
      <p>These Terms govern your use of FRIEND CHAT, a service intended to help adults meet and have conversations with randomly matched people. The service is operated by Dominik Szczerbal and Wojciech Majchrzak, ul. Śmigielska 34, 64-030 Śmigiel, Poland. By using the service, you agree to these Terms.</p>

      <h2>Eligibility and accounts</h2>
      <p>You must be at least 18 years old to use the service. You must provide accurate account information, keep your login credentials secure and promptly stop using the service if you are not eligible. Age is based on information supplied by the user; the service does not currently verify identity or age using official documents.</p>
      <p>You are responsible for activity carried out through your account. Do not impersonate another person, share your password or use another person’s account without permission.</p>

      <h2>Respectful and lawful conduct</h2>
      <p>You must not use FRIEND CHAT to threaten, harass, stalk, exploit or intimidate anyone; groom or endanger a minor; share child sexual abuse material; encourage self-harm or violence; distribute illegal material; commit fraud or phishing; spam users; or violate another person’s privacy or intellectual-property rights. Do not share intimate images, personal contact details or other sensitive information unless you understand the risks and have the other person’s consent.</p>
      <p>You must not record, copy, redistribute or publish another person’s conversation or image without their consent and any consent required by law. You are responsible for complying with the laws that apply to you.</p>

      <h2>Matching, messages and availability</h2>
      <p>Matching is random and the service does not guarantee that a conversation will be safe, suitable, uninterrupted or available. Messages are sent through the service for delivery and basic safety checks; the current application code does not save message text to its database. This does not prevent another participant from taking screenshots or recording their own screen or device.</p>
      <p>Text matching is currently implemented. The video-chat page is not yet available as a working feature. Do not assume video calls are private, recorded, moderated or end-to-end encrypted. If video chat is introduced, these Terms and the safety information will be updated before it is offered.</p>

      <h2>Safety reports and enforcement</h2>
      <p>If you encounter abuse or a safety concern, leave the conversation and contact the operators at <a href="mailto:support@friendchat.space">support@friendchat.space</a>, providing relevant details without sharing unnecessary sensitive information. The service may review submitted reports and restrict or terminate access for suspected violations. We cannot guarantee that every interaction or report will be reviewed immediately or that harmful behavior will always be prevented.</p>

      <h2>Service changes and limitations</h2>
      <p>We may change, suspend or discontinue features to maintain or protect the service. To the extent permitted by law, the service is provided without a guarantee that it will always be available, error-free or suitable for a particular purpose. Nothing in these Terms excludes rights or remedies that cannot legally be excluded.</p>

